{#-
  Body of POST /manage/case-templates/add (role cicms_2c).

  DFIR-IRIS reads the case_template_json field with json.loads(), so the case
  template has to travel as a JSON *string* inside this JSON object, and to_json
  produces exactly that - provided what it is given is still the template TEXT.

  convert_data=False is what keeps it text. The template lookup defaults to
  convert_data=True, which hands its rendered output to ast.literal_eval
  whenever it starts with '{' or '['. The template's JSON therefore came back
  as a Python dict, `| trim` turned that dict into its repr ({'name': ...}, single
  quotes), and IRIS refused it on the 2026-09-15 build with
    Invalid JSON - Expecting property name enclosed in double quotes: line 1 column 2
  Reproduced with ansible-core 2.16.14, the runner's version, with jinja2_native
  both off (the runner's default) and on. No from_json here on purpose: a
  malformed template must reach IRIS and be reported, not abort the play over a
  cosmetic resource.
-#}
{{ {'case_template_json': lookup('template', 'case_template_puc2.json.j2', convert_data=False) | trim} | to_json }}
